# Reliability
The system should continue to work correctly (performing the correct function atthe desired level of performance) even in the face of adversity.

### netflix Chaos monkey - fault tolerance
open source tool, that can test your services by literally shutting some down and check how the other behaves. they also contain a suit of other tools like a doctor monkey Gorilla monkey...

## hardware faults
Hard disks crash, RAM becomes faulty, the power grid has a blackout, someone
unplugs the wrong network cable... these are actually more common in large datacenters.  

a single-server system
requires planned downtime if you need to reboot the machine (to apply operating
system security patches, for example), whereas a system that can tolerate machine
failure can be patched one node at a time, without downtime of the entire system. 


